/* vedic-text.js — classic script; assigns to window.TD. No ES modules, so file:// works.
   Texts for the Vedic chart and astrocartography: Lagna and Moon sign (lagna:Sign, rashi:Sign), birth nakshatra
   (nak:Name), Vimshottari periods (md:Planet, ad:Major|Minor), Manglik (manglik:yes|no), Sade Sati phases
   (sadesati:rising|peak|setting) and astrocartography lines (acg:Planet:ASC|DSC|MC|IC). 186 texts.
   Written fresh for this demo; a live site edits or replaces them. */
window.TD = window.TD || {};
window.TD.VEDIC_TEXT = {"lagna:Aries":"Mars rules your rising sign, Mesha (Aries), so your body and temperament lean toward quick starts. You are likely the one who says yes first and sorts out the details on the way. Direct energy and visible courage mark how others meet you. Impatience is the cost: a project can lose its charm once the first rush fades. Life direction tends to improve when you pick fewer fights and finish them.",
"lagna:Taurus":"Venus rules your rising sign, Vrishabha (Taurus), which gives the body and manner a settled, unhurried quality. People often read you as steady and pleasant to be around. You go the direction of life slowly and by the senses: good food, comfortable rooms, work you can feel the results of. Stubbornness is the shadow, since once you have decided, a change of plan can feel like an insult.",
"lagna:Gemini":"Mercury rules your rising sign, Mithuna (Gemini), so the mind shapes the body and the temperament. You tend to look alert, talk easily and pick up a little of everything. The general direction of life moves through conversation, short trips and learning. Restlessness is the catch: a dozen open tabs, a dozen half-read books. Choosing one thread to follow for a season gives your curiosity something to build on.",
"lagna:Cancer":"The Moon rules your rising sign, Karka (Cancer), so your outward manner shifts with your mood and with the people near you. Others sense care in you before you say a word, and you often become the one who remembers birthdays and feeds the guests. Life direction is tied to home and belonging. Moodiness can make you pull back into your shell, and a safe base helps you come out again.",
"lagna:Leo":"The Sun rules your rising sign, Simha (Leo), which lends the body and temperament a natural warmth and presence. Rooms tend to notice when you walk in, and you often carry yourself with quiet dignity. Your path points toward creating something and being recognized for it. Pride is the tender spot, because criticism can sting more than you show. Generosity toward others usually earns you the respect you want.",
"lagna:Virgo":"Mercury rules your rising sign, Kanya (Virgo), so you meet the world as an observer who notices what is out of place. The body and temperament lean neat, careful and a little modest. Life direction runs through skill, useful work and being of service. Worry is the habit to watch: you can rewrite the same email four times. Letting good enough count as good gives you steadier energy.",
"lagna:Libra":"Venus rules your rising sign, Tula (Libra), which gives the body and manner a pleasing, balanced quality. People often find you easy to talk to because you instinctively look for the fair middle. Life direction runs through partnership and shared taste. Indecision is the snag: you can weigh two menu items until the waiter leaves. Trusting your first honest preference saves you a lot of time.",
"lagna:Scorpio":"Mars rules your rising sign, Vrishchika (Scorpio), so you meet the world with an intense, watchful presence. Others often sense depth in you before they know your story, and you tend to keep much of it private. The direction of life leans toward loyalty, commitment and getting to the truth underneath things. Secrecy can isolate you. Trusting one or two people fully usually lightens the load.",
"lagna:Sagittarius":"Jupiter rules your rising sign, Dhanu (Sagittarius), which gives the temperament an open, hopeful, outdoorsy feel. You tend to say what you think, often with a laugh, and others read you as friendly and frank. Life direction points toward adventure, belief and learning from far places. Bluntness is the risk, since an honest remark can land harder than intended. A little tact keeps your good humor welcome.",
"lagna:Capricorn":"Saturn rules your rising sign, Makara (Capricorn), so you present as composed, responsible and slightly reserved. Many people take you seriously from the first meeting, even when you are young. The general direction of life is climbing slowly toward real ambition, with mastery built year by year. Reserve can look like coldness to people who do not know you. Letting a few close ones see the softer side balances the effort.",
"lagna:Aquarius":"Saturn rules your rising sign, Kumbha (Aquarius), which gives you a cool, independent, slightly unusual way of meeting people. You often stand a step back and watch the group before joining. Life direction leans toward ideas, community and work that serves more than just you. Detachment is the downside: friends may wonder what you feel. Saying it out loud now and then closes that gap.",
"lagna:Pisces":"Jupiter rules your rising sign, Meena (Pisces), so you meet the world with softness and a receptive, dreamy air. People often feel understood by you without much explaining. The temperament and life direction lean toward imagination, compassion and the inner life. Boundaries can blur, and you may soak up other people's moods as if they were your own. Quiet time alone to clear your head helps you stay steady.",
"rashi:Aries":"Your Moon sits in Mesha (Aries), ruled by Mars, so the mind runs hot and fast. Feelings arrive as impulse: you want to act on a mood right away. Inner ease comes from movement, a challenge, or a clear next step. Impatience can spill into irritation when plans stall. Vedic astrology goes by this Moon sign, so it describes how you feel at the root, more than how you look.",
"rashi:Taurus":"Your Moon is in Vrishabha (Taurus), ruled by Venus, which makes the mind steady and sensory. Feelings settle through comfort: a good meal, a familiar chair, music you love. Inner ease comes from routine and things that last. Stubbornness is the flip side, because a mood can dig in and stay for days. Since Vedic practice goes by the Moon sign, this is the sign people would read first.",
"rashi:Gemini":"Mind and mood move together when the Moon is in Mithuna (Gemini), ruled by Mercury. You process feelings by talking, writing or turning them over in thought. Inner ease comes from fresh information and good conversation. The restless side keeps jumping topics, which can leave an emotion unfinished. In Vedic astrology this Moon sign is the one people go by, so it speaks to how you actually think and feel.",
"rashi:Cancer":"Your Moon is in Karka (Cancer), its own sign, ruled by the Moon itself, so feelings run deep and close to the surface. You pick up the mood in a room quickly and often care for others before yourself. Inner ease comes from home, family and being needed. Moods rise and fall like tides, and that is normal here. Vedic practice goes by this sign, so it carries extra weight.",
"rashi:Leo":"The Moon in Simha (Leo), ruled by the Sun, gives the mind a warm, proud, generous tone. Feelings want an audience, or at least some appreciation. Inner ease comes from creating something and being seen for it. Pride can bruise easily, and a slight may linger. Because Vedic astrology treats the Moon sign as your main sign, this heart-forward quality is how you are likely described.",
"rashi:Virgo":"Your Moon in Kanya (Virgo), ruled by Mercury, makes the mind precise and observant. Feelings get sorted like a drawer: noticed, labeled, fixed if possible. Inner ease comes from being useful and having things in order. The risk is worry that loops over small details at night. Since the Moon sign is the one Vedic astrology goes by, this analytical streak is central to how others understand you.",
"rashi:Libra":"Moon in Tula (Libra), ruled by Venus, gives a mind that seeks balance and harmony. Feelings often depend on the mood between you and the people close to you. Inner ease comes from fairness, beauty and a calm room. Indecision is the stumbling block, since you hear every side and agree with each. Vedic practice goes by the Moon sign, so this need for harmony is your headline trait.",
"rashi:Scorpio":"Your Moon is in Vrishchika (Scorpio), ruled by Mars, so feelings run strong and mostly out of sight. You tend to keep emotions private and remember them for a long time. Inner ease comes from trust, loyalty and a chance to go deep with a few people. Secrecy can harden into suspicion if left alone. Vedic astrology goes by the Moon sign, so this intensity defines how you are read.",
"rashi:Sagittarius":"Moon in Dhanu (Sagittarius), ruled by Jupiter, lifts the mind toward hope and big questions. Feelings tend to bounce back fast, helped by a long walk, a trip or a good argument about beliefs. Inner ease comes from freedom and a sense of meaning. Bluntness can leave others stung. In Vedic practice the Moon sign is your main sign, so optimism is the first thing people may notice.",
"rashi:Capricorn":"Your Moon sits in Makara (Capricorn), ruled by Saturn, so the mind is disciplined and keeps its feelings in check. You often show calm while carrying a lot inside. Inner ease comes from responsibility met and goals moving forward. Reserve can slide into self-criticism on a tough day. Because Vedic astrology goes by the Moon sign, this seriousness is the sign others would call yours.",
"rashi:Aquarius":"Moon in Kumbha (Aquarius), ruled by Saturn, gives a mind that likes distance, ideas and room to be different. Feelings are often examined from outside before they are shared. Inner ease comes from independence and belonging to a group with a purpose. Detachment can leave close friends guessing. Vedic practice goes by this sign, so the thinking, observing quality is the first thing a reading would stress.",
"rashi:Pisces":"Jupiter rules the Moon in Meena (Pisces), which makes the mind imaginative and absorbent. You tend to feel what others feel, sometimes before they say it. Inner ease comes from music, water, quiet and a sense of something larger. Boundaries blur, and a crowded week can leave you foggy. Vedic astrology goes by the Moon sign, so this sensitivity is the heart of your chart.",
"manglik:yes":"Manglik, or Mangal dosha, is a traditional marriage-matching check about Mars. The tradition counts Mars in the 1st, 2nd, 4th, 7th, 8th or 12th house from the Lagna or the Moon, and your chart meets it. The idea is that Mars energy, strong and direct, shows up in close partnership. Many traditions list cancellations, such as both partners having it or Mars sitting in certain signs. It is one factor among many.",
"manglik:no":"Manglik, or Mangal dosha, is a traditional matching check that looks at where Mars sits. The tradition flags Mars in the 1st, 2nd, 4th, 7th, 8th or 12th house from the Lagna or the Moon. Yours is in none of those, so the check comes back clear. That does not remove Mars from your chart. Drive, anger and courage still live in whichever house it occupies.",
"sadesati:rising":"Saturn is now in the sign before your Moon sign, which opens Sade Sati, a roughly seven and a half year span. This first phase lasts about two and a half years. Themes lean toward endings, tiredness and sleep, and letting go of what has run its course. Think of clearing a closet before a bigger project. Tradition treats it as a maturing time, not a time of misfortune.",
"sadesati:peak":"Saturn is crossing your Moon sign itself, the middle stretch of Sade Sati, lasting about two and a half years. Feelings are tested here and often come out sturdier. Responsibility feels heavier, and the mood tends toward serious and reflective. Many people find they stop pretending about what matters. Tradition treats this as a maturing time that builds inner strength, not a period of misfortune.",
"sadesati:setting":"Saturn has moved into the sign after your Moon sign, the closing phase of Sade Sati, about two and a half years long. The emphasis shifts to consolidating: practical rebuilding, clearer values, and steadying family matters and resources. It is like finishing a renovation and finally unpacking the boxes. Tradition describes the whole seven and a half years as a maturing time, never as misfortune.",
"nak:Ashwini":"Your Moon sits in the first star of the zodiac, in sidereal Aries, ruled by Ketu. Its deity is the Ashvins, twin horse-headed healers, and its symbol is a horse's head. The tendency is to move first and ask questions on the way: the friend who drives over the minute someone needs help. Speed is the gift, and a habit of starting more than you finish is the catch. Pausing long enough to see what actually needs fixing keeps that healing instinct useful instead of scattered.",
"nak:Bharani":"Someone born under the middle of sidereal Aries and the rule of Venus tends to carry things all the way through. Yama, keeper of order and limits, is the deity, and the symbol is the yoni, the womb: a project, a feeling, a family duty, held until it is complete. You feel life at full weight and hold yourself to a firm standard. The lesson is gentleness with your own limits, because bearing everything is not the same as being asked to.",
"nak:Krittika":"Fire and a blade shape this star, which runs from late Aries into early Taurus under the Sun. Agni, the fire, is the deity. You cut through fuzziness the way a sharp knife does, and people often come to you for the honest read of a situation. That clarity can turn into a sharp tongue when you are tired. Warmth is the other use of fire: keep the edge for the problem, not for the person sitting across from you.",
"nak:Rohini":"One of the most comfort-loving stars, this one sits in sidereal Taurus and is ruled by the Moon. Prajapati, the creator, is the deity, and an ox cart is the symbol: something built to carry a load and bring a harvest home. You tend to make things grow, whether that is a garden, a home, or a following. Attachment is the shadow side. Holding onto what is lovely can crowd out room for what is changing.",
"nak:Mrigashira":"Always sniffing the air, the deer's head of Mrigashira marks a searcher. The star straddles late Taurus and early Gemini under Mars, and its deity is Soma, the Moon and its nectar. You are curious, a little restless, and happiest while hunting for the next interesting thing. Mars gives the search some drive. The risk is browsing forever, with twelve tabs open and no decision. Picking one trail and following it a while is how the search pays off.",
"nak:Ardra":"Rain after a heavy sky is the image for Ardra, the first half of sidereal Gemini, ruled by Rahu. Rudra, the storm, is its deity and a teardrop its symbol. Feelings build, break, and leave the air cleaner. You may cry easily, think intensely, and keep wanting to understand why things hurt. That depth is a strength. Many people born here turn hard weather into insight, and the clearing after the storm is where your best work tends to begin.",
"nak:Punarvasu":"Return is the meaning of the name: getting back to the good place after a setback. The star crosses from late Gemini into early Cancer under Jupiter, with Aditi, the boundless mother, as deity and a quiver of arrows as symbol. You tend to bounce back, to forgive, and to trust that another round is coming. Like a full quiver, you can try again. The watch point is staying generous without becoming the one everyone leans on and nobody checks on.",
"nak:Pushya":"Often called the nourishing star, Pushya sits in sidereal Cancer and is ruled by Saturn. Its deity is Brihaspati, teacher of the gods, and its symbol a cow's udder. You tend to feed others, with food, advice, or steady presence, and you do it without much fuss. Saturn adds discipline, so the care is dependable instead of showy. The lesson is receiving: the teacher also needs a teacher, and a full udder still needs rest.",
"nak:Ashlesha":"A coiled serpent is held energy, and that is the feel of Ashlesha, the last stretch of sidereal Cancer under Mercury. Its deity is the Nagas, serpent beings. It often shows as deep intuition, sharp reading of people, and a private inner world. You notice what others miss. Because feelings run deep, you may keep them close until you trust someone. Learning to uncoil gradually, letting trusted people see what you sense, turns that watchfulness into real closeness.",
"nak:Magha":"Inheritance runs through this star, which opens sidereal Leo and is ruled by Ketu. The Pitris, the ancestors, are its deity and a royal throne its symbol. Family stories, lineage, and a role you grew into all feature. You carry yourself with natural dignity, and people may treat you as the one who sets the tone. Ketu keeps part of you detached from the crown. The growth is earning the seat by serving the people around it.",
"nak:Purva Phalguni":"Rest and pleasure are built into the symbol here, the front legs of a bed. The star sits in the middle of sidereal Leo under Venus, and its deity is Bhaga, god of delight and fortune. You tend to enjoy life openly and make others feel welcome at the table. Creativity and romance come easily. The catch is that a love of ease can slow ambition, so scheduling rest as a reward, not an escape, suits you.",
"nak:Uttara Phalguni":"Keeping a promise and remembering the favor come naturally to those born here. The star stretches from late Leo into early Virgo under the Sun. Aryaman, god of friendship and agreements, is the deity, and the back legs of a bed are the symbol, the support that holds the frame steady. People trust you with arrangements. The risk is carrying more than your share to protect a bond, so say plainly what you need in return.",
"nak:Hasta":"Skill with the hands is the classic image of Hasta, an open hand in the first half of sidereal Virgo, ruled by the Moon. Savitar, the Sun as inspirer, is the deity. You tend to read a room and then do something useful about it: crafting, fixing, typing fast, a knack for the practical gesture. Humor is a hidden strength here. The shadow is fussing over details, so letting good enough count helps.",
"nak:Chitra":"Design, finish, and how a thing looks when it is done well catch your eye. Chitra runs from late Virgo into early Libra under Mars, and Mars gives you the drive to build it. Tvashtar, also called Vishvakarma, the divine craftsman, is the deity, and a bright jewel the symbol. People may see you as striking even when you are quiet. The watch point is polish over substance: the finished piece should shine because it works.",
"nak:Swati":"Bending without breaking is the gift of a young shoot swaying in the wind. Swati sits in sidereal Libra, ruled by Rahu, with Vayu, the wind, as deity. You value independence and adjust to circumstances with a lot of grace. Trade, negotiation, and travel often appeal. Rahu adds a restless appetite for something new. The task is rooting: a shoot that sways but never grows deeper stays small, so choosing a few places to stay put matters.",
"nak:Vishakha":"Ambition and focus are joined in this star, which crosses late Libra into early Scorpio under Jupiter. Indra and Agni share it as deities, a leader's reach with a fire's concentration, and the symbol is a triumphal arch. You tend to set a goal and walk toward it through whatever is in the way, often with strong persuasion. Passing under the arch is the reward. The lesson is sharing the win, since the single-minded stretch can leave companions behind.",
"nak:Anuradha":"A lotus opens clean from muddy water, and Anuradha, in the first half of sidereal Scorpio under Saturn, works that way. Mitra, god of friendship and devotion, is its deity. You build lasting friendships, often across differences, and you show up for people with quiet consistency. Saturn gives patience. The shadow is loyalty that outlasts its welcome, so noticing when a bond has stopped feeding you matters as much as keeping it.",
"nak:Jyeshtha":"Seniority is the theme here, marked by a round earring or umbrella. The star closes sidereal Scorpio under Mercury, and Indra, chief of the gods, is its deity. You tend to be the elder in the room, whatever your age: the one others look to for protection and a clear call. Mercury adds a sharp mind. The growth lies in letting authority rest on care instead of rank, and in asking for help before the load gets heavy.",
"nak:Mula":"Roots are the symbol, and this star digs to the bottom of things. It opens sidereal Sagittarius under Ketu, and its deity is Nirriti, who clears away what has decayed. You want the real source, not the surface story, and you may go through a few rounds of letting go before something solid grows. Clearing is renewal, not loss. Healthy roots make room for the next season of growth.",
"nak:Purva Ashadha":"Confidence that is hard to discourage marks this star, in the middle of sidereal Sagittarius under Venus. Apas, the waters, is the deity, and a winnowing fan the symbol, the tool that separates grain from husk. You tend to be persuasive and refreshing to be around. Water finds its way, and so do you. The practice is sorting what is worth keeping from what is noise, including opinions you picked up along the way.",
"nak:Uttara Ashadha":"Staying power more than flash is how you tend to win, much like an elephant's tusk, strong and unhurried. The star runs from late Sagittarius into early Capricorn under the Sun, and the Vishvadevas, the universal gods, are its deity. Your principles are not for sale, and others notice that you keep going after the cheering stops. The watch point is rigidity: a tusk is hard to turn, so asking whether the plan still serves everyone is worth the minute.",
"nak:Shravana":"Listening is the skill, and the ear is the symbol. The star sits in the first half of sidereal Capricorn under the Moon, with Vishnu, the preserver, as deity. You take in what people say, absorb knowledge, and pass it on in a way others can use, which often makes a good teacher, counselor, or keeper of records. The risk is soaking up everyone's concerns until your own go unheard, so quiet time to process belongs on your list.",
"nak:Dhanishta":"A drum sets a group moving together, and that is the pull of Dhanishta, running from late Capricorn into early Aquarius under Mars. Its deity is the eight Vasus, gods of abundance. You tend to have rhythm and drive, in music, in sport, or in the pace you set at work. Others fall in step with you. Mars can make you brisk with those who are slower, so matching the beat to the room helps the whole band play.",
"nak:Shatabhisha":"The empty circle is left empty so something can be shared inside it, and the phrase a hundred healers hints at that. The star sits in sidereal Aquarius under Rahu, with Varuna, lord of the cosmic waters, as deity. You tend to be private, unconventional, and drawn to research, cures for the world's ailments, or the wide open sky. Solitude restores you. The invitation is to let a few people in.",
"nak:Purva Bhadrapada":"Two pulls live side by side here: the idealist and the private, intense thinker. The star runs from late Aquarius into early Pisces under Jupiter, and its symbol is a two-faced figure. Aja Ekapada, the one-footed goat, a fiery form, is the deity. That doubleness gives passion for causes and a taste for deep questions. Fire here means transformation, not harm. Letting both faces speak, not choosing between them, is where your fullest voice tends to come from.",
"nak:Uttara Bhadrapada":"Calm under pressure is the signature of a patient, still center that others lean on. The star sits in the first half of sidereal Pisces under Saturn, which gives endurance. Ahir Budhnya, the serpent of the deep, is the deity, and the back legs of a bed the symbol, standing for depth and rest. The depth can read as distance, so a word about what is going on inside you helps people feel close.",
"nak:Revati":"Last of the twenty-seven, this star closes sidereal Pisces under Mercury. Pushan, the nourisher and guide of travellers, is the deity, and a fish is the symbol, sometimes a drum. You tend to look after those in transition: the new hire, the traveler, the friend between chapters. Gentleness is natural to you, and so is a dreamy streak. Finishing things well is the lesson of the final star, so giving your own journeys a proper ending matters.",
"md:Ketu":"Seven years that tend to loosen your grip. Ketu is the planet of detachment, and its chapter often feels like a long exhale. Things you chased for years may lose their shine, and you may care less about being noticed. Many people turn toward quiet study, spiritual questions or simply more time alone. Skills that come naturally can surface without effort. The risk is drifting or feeling unmoored. The invitation is to let go of what is finished and keep what is true.",
"md:Venus":"Twenty years, the longest chapter in the Vimshottari cycle, given to Venus. Love, partnership, art, beauty and comfort move to the front of your attention. You may care more about how your home looks, who you share your time with and what makes an ordinary day pleasant. Creative and social gifts tend to find room. The pull toward ease can turn into over-indulgence or dependence on approval. The work is to enjoy this fully while keeping your own values steady.",
"md:Sun":"A short, bright six years centered on identity. The Sun governs self, authority and recognition, so questions of who you are and what you stand for tend to come up. Father figures, bosses and mentors may loom larger, for better or for worse. Confidence can grow when you take clear responsibility. Pride and a need to be seen as right can also get loud. The chapter rewards people who lead by example instead of by volume.",
"md:Moon":"Ten years where the inner weather matters most. The Moon rules the mind and feelings, so moods, memory and the need for comfort set the tone. Mother figures, home life and your relationship with the public or with groups of people often come into focus. Sensitivity is a strength here, since you read a room well. It can also mean ups and downs. Steady routines and a safe place to land help this period feel nourishing.",
"md:Mars":"Seven years with a lot of fuel in the tank. Mars brings energy, courage and competitive drive, and many people feel a push to act instead of wait. Siblings, land, property and physical effort are common themes. You may find that you want to claim ground, whether that is a project, a space or a position. Impatience and friction with others can flare. The chapter rewards focus: pick the battle worth fighting and put your energy there.",
"md:Rahu":"Eighteen years of reaching for more. Rahu is the hungry, restless node, linked with ambition, the unconventional and anything foreign or new. Many people feel pulled to leave familiar paths, try unusual fields, move away or chase something that fascinates them. Change can arrive quickly and without warning. The shadow side is obsession and never feeling satisfied. The work is to follow genuine curiosity while staying honest with yourself about what you actually want.",
"md:Jupiter":"Sixteen years that lean toward growth. Jupiter brings wisdom, teachers, faith and a stronger sense of ethics, or dharma. Learning, mentors and questions about meaning tend to matter more. Children and the next generation, whether your own or others you guide, can become a focus. Optimism often rises. The trap is taking too much on or assuming things will work out without effort. Used well, this chapter lets you build something broad and generous.",
"md:Saturn":"Nineteen years of steady, serious work. Saturn asks for discipline, patience and duty, and it tends to reward effort slowly. Responsibilities often grow, and you may feel the weight of time more than in lighter periods. Service, craft and long commitments matter here. It can feel heavy or lonely at moments, but the habits you build tend to last. Nothing in this chapter is quick, and that is the point: what you earn is yours.",
"md:Mercury":"Seventeen years where the mind runs the show. Mercury favors intellect, speech, learning and trade, so reading, writing, negotiating and skill with detail tend to get attention. You may take up new subjects, pick up side projects or find that your words carry more weight. Restlessness and overthinking come with the territory, and so does scattered focus. The chapter works best when you pick a few topics to master and let curiosity serve them.",
"ad:Ketu|Ketu":"The opening months of the Ketu chapter, about five months, show its themes with nothing diluted. Detachment, a taste for solitude and quiet insight run strong. You may notice yourself stepping back from things that used to pull at you. Natural skills can show up without effort. It is a clean start to a period of letting go.",
"ad:Ketu|Venus":"Warmth enters the Ketu years for about 1.2 years. The detached, inward mood meets love, art and comfort, so relationships can feel oddly both close and distant. You may want beauty that is simple and sincere rather than showy. Pleasure and spiritual calm sit side by side, and the question is how to hold both.",
"ad:Ketu|Sun":"A brief stretch of about four months where the Sun puts identity into Ketu's detached chapter. You may ask who you are once recognition stops mattering so much. Father figures or authority can be a subject of reflection. Confidence grows quietly, from inside, rather than from applause.",
"ad:Ketu|Moon":"Around seven months where the Moon makes Ketu's detachment emotional. Feelings, memory and the pull of home and family may surface while part of you wants distance. Mood can swing between needing people and needing space. Gentle routines and a quiet home help the sensitivity settle into insight.",
"ad:Ketu|Mars":"A spark of energy lands in the Ketu chapter for about five months. The usual calm detachment meets drive and restlessness, so you may feel both pulled to act and unsure it matters. Competition and property questions can feel oddly pointless or oddly sharp. Physical activity gives that energy somewhere useful to go.",
"ad:Ketu|Rahu":"Both lunar nodes meet here for about 1.1 years, a period of strong contrasts. Ambition and fascination run into letting go and doubt, so you may chase something new while questioning whether you want it. Sudden changes and unconventional paths are common themes. Sorting real hunger from restlessness is the main task.",
"ad:Ketu|Jupiter":"A wiser, more hopeful tone lifts the Ketu chapter for about eleven months. Detachment feels less bare. Teachers, books and questions of faith and ethics can feel unusually meaningful, and spiritual interests often deepen. Letting go feels less like loss and more like making room for something larger.",
"ad:Ketu|Saturn":"Structure arrives in the Ketu years for about 1.1 years. The inward mood meets duty and patience, so quiet, disciplined work comes naturally. You may feel serious, a little solitary and ready to commit to something unglamorous. Slow, lasting progress is the theme, and the pace may feel heavy but steady.",
"ad:Ketu|Mercury":"The mind gets sharper in the Ketu chapter for about twelve months. Detachment turns analytical: you may study, write or think deeply about things others miss. Skill with detail and speech come easily, though thoughts may also spin. Learning for its own sake, with no audience in mind, fits this stretch well.",
"ad:Venus|Ketu":"A cooler, quieter thread cuts through the Venus chapter for about 1.2 years. Love, comfort and beauty meet detachment, so you may feel less hooked by pleasure and more interested in what is real. Relationships can feel distant or deeply simple. Letting go of what no longer satisfies makes room for something more honest.",
"ad:Venus|Venus":"The opening of the Venus chapter, about 3.3 years, with its themes at full strength. Love, partnership, art, beauty and comfort move to the center of life. Taste sharpens, and the wish for harmony grows. It is a long, rich stretch where enjoyment is a real priority, as long as it does not slide into excess.",
"ad:Venus|Sun":"The Sun enters the Venus chapter for about one year. Comfort and relationships meet a stronger sense of self, so you may want to be seen and respected, not only liked. Creative work can gain confidence. Watch for pride bumping against a partner's need for equal footing.",
"ad:Venus|Moon":"The Moon softens the Venus chapter for about 1.7 years. Feelings and the wish for comfort rise together, making home, family and close bonds central. You may want to nest, nurture and be nurtured. Moods can follow the people around you, so steady routines help.",
"ad:Venus|Mars":"Heat enters the Venus chapter for about 1.2 years. Desire and drive meet taste and affection, so attraction, creative energy and a wish to act on what you love grow stronger. Passion can also bring friction in close bonds. Channel it into projects and honest conversation.",
"ad:Venus|Rahu":"Across about three years, worldly hunger stretches the Venus chapter. Taste and affection meet restlessness, so you may be drawn to glamorous, foreign or unconventional people and settings. Fascination can run high, and so can the urge to want more than you have. Keep checking what you value beneath the shine.",
"ad:Venus|Jupiter":"Generosity widens the Venus chapter for about 2.7 years. Love and comfort gain wisdom and faith. Teachers, shared beliefs and growth through relationships tend to matter. Enjoyment feels more meaningful, though easy abundance can tempt you toward excess. A gracious, expansive stretch.",
"ad:Venus|Saturn":"Pleasure meets duty across about 3.2 years of the Venus chapter. Commitments, loyalty and long-term bonds get tested and deepened. Comfort may come more slowly and feel earned. Patience with relationships pays off here, even when things look plain.",
"ad:Venus|Mercury":"Talk and skill enter the Venus chapter for about 2.8 years. Art, charm and partnership become things you can discuss, write about or trade in. Conversation is part of romance, and design or craft with fine detail comes easily. Overthinking a feeling is the common snag.",
"ad:Sun|Ketu":"A quiet, inward note opens the Sun chapter for about four months. The drive for recognition meets a pull toward detachment, so you may wonder what you actually want to be known for. Authority can feel hollow. Inner confidence, rather than applause, is what gets built.",
"ad:Sun|Venus":"Charm softens the Sun chapter for about one year. Confidence meets warmth, so being seen and being liked go hand in hand. Relationships, art and comfort may support your sense of self. Enjoy the warmth, but guard against needing constant admiration.",
"ad:Sun|Sun":"The Sun chapter begins with its own energy at full strength for about four months. Identity, authority and the wish for recognition are front and center. You may take on a clearer role or speak up more. Pride and stubbornness are the risk, while clear leadership is the gift.",
"ad:Sun|Moon":"The Moon gives the Sun chapter an emotional side for about six months. Self-expression meets feelings, family and the public, so your inner mood shapes how confident you feel. Mother and father figures may both come into view. Balance what you want to show with what you honestly feel.",
"ad:Sun|Mars":"Fire is added to the Sun chapter for about four months. Confidence turns into action, competition and a willingness to push forward. You may want to lead, argue your case or claim ground. Impatience with others is the weak spot, and focused effort is the strength.",
"ad:Sun|Rahu":"Ambition stirs the Sun chapter for about eleven months. The wish for recognition meets worldly hunger, so unconventional routes to status look tempting. Foreign settings or sudden shifts in standing are common themes. Beware chasing the spotlight at the cost of your own steadiness.",
"ad:Sun|Jupiter":"Wisdom and generosity lift the Sun chapter for about ten months. Authority gains perspective. Mentors, teachers and questions of ethics shape how you lead. Confidence feels better grounded in values. A good stretch for guiding others, as long as optimism does not turn into overreach.",
"ad:Sun|Saturn":"Duty weighs on the Sun chapter for about eleven months. Self-confidence meets limits, so recognition comes through patient work rather than quick praise. Authority figures may feel strict. It can be a sober stretch, and the self-respect built here tends to last.",
"ad:Sun|Mercury":"Identity finds its voice in the Sun chapter for about ten months. Speaking, writing, teaching and negotiating can bring recognition. Clever, detailed work gets noticed. The snag is talking over others, so listen as well as lead.",
"ad:Moon|Ketu":"A pull inward opens the Moon chapter for about seven months. Feelings meet detachment, so you may feel strangely distant from comfort or home while turning toward reflection. Memory and old attachments can surface for release. Quiet time helps the sensitivity become insight.",
"ad:Moon|Venus":"Sweetness settles into the Moon chapter for about 1.7 years. Emotional needs find comfort in love, beauty and gentle company. Home and close bonds feel warmer, and the public may respond to your charm. Soft living is the gift, and drifting into comfort for its own sake is the trap.",
"ad:Moon|Sun":"The Sun brightens the Moon chapter for about six months. Feelings meet a stronger sense of self, so you may feel more visible and clear about what you need. Parents, especially father figures, can take emotional weight. Confidence grows when you trust what you feel.",
"ad:Moon|Moon":"The Moon chapter opens with its own themes at full strength for about ten months. Mood, memory, home and the need for comfort run strong. You read people closely and may be moved by the public mood. Gentle routines and a safe space steady the tides.",
"ad:Moon|Mars":"Energy rises in the Moon chapter for about seven months. Feelings turn into action, and tempers or enthusiasm may come quickly. Home, land and siblings can draw energy. Courage in protecting what you love is a strength, while snapping at people nearby is the risk.",
"ad:Moon|Rahu":"Restlessness unsettles the Moon chapter for about 1.5 years. Emotions meet worldly hunger and fascination, so big wants and unusual interests grow. Home may change or feel foreign. The mind can race with new possibilities. Slow breaths and grounded habits keep the feelings clear.",
"ad:Moon|Jupiter":"Kindness and perspective bless the Moon chapter for about 1.3 years. Feelings gain faith and optimism. Mother figures, teachers and a sense of meaning at home can feel supportive. Generosity toward others deepens your own comfort.",
"ad:Moon|Saturn":"A cooler, heavier note enters the Moon chapter for about 1.6 years. Feelings meet duty and restraint, so emotional life can feel serious or lonely at times. Responsibility toward family or the public may grow. Steady routines and patience turn the heaviness into maturity.",
"ad:Moon|Mercury":"Feelings find words in the Moon chapter for about 1.4 years. Talking, writing and learning help you process the inside. Home life may involve plans, paperwork or trade. The mind is active, and the risk is worrying in circles rather than resting.",
"ad:Mars|Ketu":"A short stretch where the usual push loosens. The drive of the Mars chapter is still there, but Ketu turns it inward, so you may care less about winning and more about what you do well without trying. Competitions can feel pointless, and letting go of a fight can bring clarity.",
"ad:Mars|Venus":"Energy meets warmth, and effort starts going toward things you enjoy. Courage shows up in affection: saying the honest thing to a partner, or putting work into a home that feels good. The competitive streak softens into taste and charm, and a project may be about beauty as much as results.",
"ad:Mars|Sun":"A brief stretch where drive wants a face and a name. Mars energy runs through the Sun's themes of confidence and authority, so you may push to lead, to be recognized, or to hold your own with a father figure or boss. Pride and action pull the same way, which helps and can also bristle.",
"ad:Mars|Moon":"Action gets filtered through mood. The courage and restlessness of the Mars chapter meet the Moon's need for comfort, so energy rises and dips with how settled you feel. Home, a mother figure or public opinion can matter more than usual. Doing something physical often steadies the mind better than thinking it over.",
"ad:Mars|Mars":"The chapter opens at full strength. Energy, courage and the urge to compete are all in the foreground, along with matters of siblings, land and property. There is plenty of fuel and little buffer, so impatience arrives fast. Pointing the push at one clear goal works better than scattering it.",
"ad:Mars|Rahu":"Drive gets a hungry, restless edge. Rahu pulls the Mars chapter toward the unconventional and foreign, so ambition may aim at something new, unfamiliar or outside your usual circle. Courage and fascination feed each other, which can be exciting and also scattered. Check that the goal is really yours.",
"ad:Mars|Jupiter":"Energy finds a purpose. Jupiter brings teachers, ethics and a wider view to the Mars chapter, so effort tends to go toward something you believe in, such as a skill, a cause or children in your care. Courage is steadier here, and competition feels more like growth than a fight.",
"ad:Mars|Saturn":"Heat meets weight. Saturn asks the energy of the Mars chapter to work within limits: schedules, duties, slow building. Frustration can show up when action feels held back, yet patient effort on land, property or a long task tends to last. It is demanding, and it teaches how to pace strength.",
"ad:Mars|Mercury":"Energy goes into the mind and the mouth. Mercury gives the Mars chapter a sharp, busy edge: quick learning, brisk speech, deals and detail work. Arguments come easily, so word choice matters. Courage here often looks like asking the direct question, or finishing a technical job others avoid.",
"ad:Rahu|Ketu":"Two shadow points meet, and the chase loosens. The hunger of the Rahu chapter runs into Ketu's detachment, so some goals lose their shine while quieter insight grows. It can feel like confusion or like relief. Skills picked up earlier tend to resurface, and dropping one ambition can clear room.",
"ad:Rahu|Venus":"Ambition turns toward pleasure and connection. Venus makes love, art, beauty and comfort the thing to chase in the Rahu chapter, often through unusual or foreign tastes. Fascination with a person or a look is common. Enjoy it, and notice when wanting more stops feeling like enough.",
"ad:Rahu|Sun":"A short push for recognition. The Sun puts self, authority and confidence at the front of the Rahu chapter, so the hunger for more focuses on standing and on how a father figure or leader sees you. Ambition looks bold. Ego and appetite feed each other, so watch how you treat others.",
"ad:Rahu|Moon":"Hunger meets feeling. The Moon brings mind, home and the public into the Rahu chapter, so restlessness often shows up as mood swings, a pull toward unfamiliar places, or concern with reputation. Comfort can feel just out of reach. Steady routines and a trusted person help the inner weather settle.",
"ad:Rahu|Mars":"Ambition gets muscle. Mars gives the Rahu chapter drive, nerve and a competitive streak, so the pull toward something new comes with a push to act on it now. Courage is high, and so is impatience, especially around siblings, property or rivals. Pick one target and choose the unconventional route on purpose.",
"ad:Rahu|Rahu":"Its own themes at full volume: ambition, fascination, the foreign and unusual, and sudden turns. Nothing tempers the hunger yet, so wanting can outrun judgment. This long stretch rewards curiosity and a willingness to be different, and it asks you to question which wants are really yours.",
"ad:Rahu|Jupiter":"Ambition meets wisdom. Jupiter brings teachers, ethics and faith to the Rahu chapter, so the hunger to expand gets guidance. Growth often comes through study, mentors, children or beliefs that reach beyond your own culture. The risk is overconfidence: big hopes need a sense of what is reasonable.",
"ad:Rahu|Saturn":"Fascination meets patience. Saturn asks the big wants of the Rahu chapter to be built through duty, discipline and slow work. It is a demanding, grounded stretch: shortcuts feel closed, and ambition lasts only if it is earned. Results come slower and sturdier than the sudden change Rahu offers alone.",
"ad:Rahu|Mercury":"Ambition runs through the mind. Mercury gives the Rahu chapter a talent for learning, speaking, trade and detail, often with new technology or foreign ideas. Clever plans arrive quickly. The watch point is overthinking or talking yourself into something. Writing things down and checking facts keeps a sharp mind honest.",
"ad:Jupiter|Ketu":"A quiet, inward turn inside a generous chapter. Ketu loosens the Jupiter focus on teachers, children and growth, and detachment brings insight rather than expansion. Beliefs get tested and simplified. Wisdom that came easily before may feel clearer now. Some things feel finished, and that makes space.",
"ad:Jupiter|Venus":"Growth gets sweet. Venus brings love, art, beauty and comfort into the Jupiter chapter, so wisdom and enjoyment travel together. Relationships, creativity and a pleasant home are often in focus, and teachers or children add warmth. A long, easy stretch. The cost is drifting into comfort when there is more to learn.",
"ad:Jupiter|Sun":"Faith finds a spokesperson. The Sun gives the Jupiter chapter confidence and standing, so beliefs and learning step into the open. Father figures, mentors and people in authority matter more. Recognition for what you know is a theme. It is a brief stretch, good for leading with principle rather than pride.",
"ad:Jupiter|Moon":"Wisdom becomes personal. The Moon turns the Jupiter chapter toward feelings, home, mother figures and the public, so faith and growth are felt in the gut as much as understood. Caring for others comes naturally, and so does generosity. Moods can swell with optimism, so give big plans a night's sleep.",
"ad:Jupiter|Mars":"Faith gets legs. Mars gives the Jupiter chapter energy and courage, so beliefs turn into action: teaching, defending a cause, building on land or property, or competing for what you value. Zeal is the strength and the risk. Direct it with the ethics Jupiter brings, and play fair.",
"ad:Jupiter|Rahu":"Faith meets appetite. Rahu stirs ambition and fascination into the Jupiter chapter, so growth reaches toward foreign ideas, unusual teachers and larger-than-usual goals. Sudden shifts of belief or direction are common themes. The stretch is long and rewards curiosity. Keep ethics in view, since big wants can bend principles.",
"ad:Jupiter|Jupiter":"Full strength from the first day of the chapter. Wisdom, teachers, children, growth and faith in what is right all sit in the foreground with nothing to temper them. Generosity and optimism come easily, and so does taking on too much. A good stretch for learning and guiding, if the promises stay realistic.",
"ad:Jupiter|Saturn":"Faith meets structure. Saturn asks the big hopes of the Jupiter chapter to carry real responsibility, so growth comes through discipline, duty and slow, practical work. Teachers may be strict, and optimism gets tested against what is workable. It can feel heavy, and it gives beliefs a durable frame.",
"ad:Jupiter|Mercury":"Wisdom picks up a pen. Mercury gives the Jupiter chapter a talent for explaining, learning, trade and fine detail, so big ideas get organized into words and plans. Teaching, writing and study fit naturally here. The risk is clever talk running ahead of conviction, so check that action matches speech.",
"ad:Saturn|Ketu":"Duty meets detachment. Ketu loosens the grip of the Saturn chapter's discipline, so some obligations feel hollow and others become clear. It is a stretch for simplifying, trimming what no longer earns its place, and quiet insight into your work. Results stay slow, but the weight feels less personal.",
"ad:Saturn|Venus":"Hard work gets company. Venus brings love, beauty and comfort into the long duty of the Saturn chapter, so effort is balanced by pleasure and partnership. Relationships are deepened by steady commitment rather than romance alone. Art or craft practiced slowly can pay off. Comfort should not become a way to avoid effort.",
"ad:Saturn|Sun":"Duty meets identity. The Sun puts self, authority and recognition into the Saturn chapter, so pressure to prove yourself rises, often with a father figure or boss in the picture. Confidence is built slowly here, through responsibility carried well. Ego and humility pull against each other, and this shorter stretch tests both.",
"ad:Saturn|Moon":"Work is felt in the heart. The Moon brings mood, home and mother figures into the Saturn chapter, so duties can weigh on the mind and comfort feels earned. Emotional steadiness is the lesson: routines, family obligations and care for others. Rest matters. Feelings tend to mature rather than vanish.",
"ad:Saturn|Mars":"Discipline meets drive. Mars adds energy and courage to the Saturn chapter, so there is stamina for hard physical or technical work, and frustration when progress is slow. It is a demanding pairing where pace matters. Controlled effort on property, projects or rivals lasts longer than bursts.",
"ad:Saturn|Rahu":"Patience meets hunger. Rahu stirs worldly ambition into the Saturn chapter, so there is a pull to leap ahead while duty insists on the slow route. The friction is the work: ambition tested by realism, unconventional paths held to real standards. A long, demanding stretch where steady effort outlasts shortcuts.",
"ad:Saturn|Jupiter":"Discipline finds a guide. Jupiter brings teachers, ethics and a wider outlook into the Saturn chapter, easing some of its weight. Hard work gets meaning, and responsibility can turn into mentoring or teaching. Growth is steady rather than dramatic. Faith and duty support each other, provided optimism does not skip the work.",
"ad:Saturn|Saturn":"Full weight from the first day of the chapter. Discipline, patience, duty and slow results are all in the foreground, with no other planet to soften them. It is a long, demanding stretch about building and about what you can sustain. Small, consistent habits count more than big efforts, and rest is part of the work.",
"ad:Saturn|Mercury":"Duty gets organized. Mercury brings intellect, speech and detail into the Saturn chapter, so work turns toward planning, records, learning a trade and careful communication. Skill with detail builds slowly into reputation. Worry and overthinking can crowd in, so break the load into lists and take one task at a time.",
"ad:Mercury|Ketu":"The sharp mind goes quiet. Ketu loosens the Mercury love of talk and detail, so some words and studies lose their pull while a deeper kind of insight comes forward. Skills that came naturally may feel effortless. Silence and focus serve better than debate, and letting go of a topic can feel like relief.",
"ad:Mercury|Venus":"Thinking turns sociable. Venus brings love, art and comfort into the Mercury chapter, so conversation, design, writing and charm come easily. Learning goes down better when it is enjoyable, and relationships are shaped by talk. A long, pleasant stretch. The watch point is spending effort on being liked rather than being exact.",
"ad:Mercury|Sun":"Ideas want an audience. The Sun brings confidence and authority into the Mercury chapter, so speech and learning step into the light. Recognition for your thinking, or an exchange with a father figure or senior, is a theme. A brief stretch, good for presenting clearly, though pride in being right can limit listening.",
"ad:Mercury|Moon":"Thoughts follow feelings. The Moon colors the Mercury chapter with mood, home and the public, so words and ideas are shaped by how settled you feel. Empathy sharpens conversation, and a mother figure may be central. Memory and imagination are rich, though worry can replay. Talking with someone calm helps.",
"ad:Mercury|Mars":"Words get an edge. Mars adds energy and courage to the Mercury chapter, so thinking becomes quick, direct and competitive. Debate, technical problems and deals are favored, and so are sharp remarks. Speed is the strength and the hazard: pause before sending the message. A short stretch, well suited to finishing things.",
"ad:Mercury|Rahu":"Curiosity turns restless and ambitious. Rahu pulls the Mercury chapter toward unconventional ideas, foreign places, new technology and sudden shifts of plan. Learning can be fast and absorbing, even obsessive. Clever strategies appeal, so verify facts and read terms carefully. Fascination points at what to study, not at what is true.",
"ad:Mercury|Jupiter":"The learner meets the teacher. Jupiter brings wisdom, mentors and ethics into the Mercury chapter, so information deepens into understanding. Study, teaching, writing and advice are well placed, and children can be part of the picture. Detail gets a purpose. Lecturing when listening is needed is the thing to watch.",
"ad:Mercury|Saturn":"The mind gets serious. Saturn asks the quick thinking of the Mercury chapter to slow down and prove itself through discipline, structure and careful, repeated practice. Learning feels harder but sticks. Speech becomes more reserved, and responsibilities weigh on the mind. Mastery of a skill is built here rather than shown off.",
"ad:Mercury|Mercury":"Its own voice, at the start of the chapter. Intellect, speech, learning, trade and skill with detail are all at full strength, with nothing else shading them. Curiosity is high and so is scattered attention. Many threads get started, so choose a few worth finishing. Clear writing and honest talk are the best use of it.",
"acg:Sun:ASC":"Places on this line tend to make you feel more like yourself. Confidence comes a little easier, and people notice you sooner than they might elsewhere. Living or travelling near it, you may find your energy steadier and your sense of purpose clearer. The catch is leaning on applause, so it helps to check what you actually want.",
"acg:Sun:DSC":"Near this line, the people you meet one to one often seem bright, confident or a bit larger than life. You may attract partners and colleagues who carry the spotlight, and you may hand it to them too easily. Living or travelling here can teach you to share attention instead of orbiting it.",
"acg:Sun:MC":"Places on this line put your name and your work in clear view. Living or travelling near it, you may find it natural to take the lead, be recognised and speak with authority in a room. Visibility is the gift. The test is whether the title you chase still fits who you are.",
"acg:Sun:IC":"A warm, steady sense of belonging can gather around this line. Living or travelling near it, you may feel your identity settle from the inside, and family or home life may become a source of pride and vitality. The risk is a household where one strong personality, perhaps yours, sets every tone.",
"acg:Moon:ASC":"Feelings sit close to the surface in places on this line. You may come across as gentler, more approachable and easier to read, and moods can shift with the weather or the crowd. Living or travelling near it often brings a stronger need for comfort, familiar food and a few people who feel like family.",
"acg:Moon:DSC":"Close one-to-one bonds tend to feel nurturing near this line. You may attract people who look after you, or who need looking after, and meetings can carry a family-like warmth. Living or travelling here asks you to notice when caring becomes mothering, and to say plainly what you need back.",
"acg:Moon:MC":"Along this line, a public role links your public role with care, instinct and the everyday needs of ordinary people. Work that feeds, shelters, teaches or listens may find an audience. Living or travelling near it, you may feel visible when your feelings are, so a private place to recover matters.",
"acg:Moon:IC":"This is one of the homiest lines on the map. Living or travelling near it often stirs memories, family feeling and a wish to nest. Rooms may feel softer and evenings slower. Because old emotions rise easily here, it helps to give them time and company instead of rushing past them.",
"acg:Mercury:ASC":"Your mind runs quicker in places on this line. You may come across as curious, chatty and sharp, and conversations start easily with strangers. Living or travelling near it, ideas, notes and errands multiply. The downside is a restless head that skims, so choosing one thing to finish keeps the buzz useful.",
"acg:Mercury:DSC":"Talk is the main event near this line. The people you meet one to one tend to be witty, informative and happy to trade ideas, and partnerships may grow through letters, calls and long chats. Living or travelling here, watch for clever people who say more than they commit to.",
"acg:Mercury:MC":"Along this line, public life rewards clear speech, writing and sharp reasoning in your public life. Teaching, selling, reporting, negotiating or running a small business of ideas can all find a footing. Living or travelling near it, you may be known as the person who explains things well.",
"acg:Mercury:IC":"Near this line, the home tends to fill with books, screens, notes and conversation. Living or travelling here may bring back family stories, or a wish to study your own roots. Inner life gets chatty, so it helps to write thoughts down before they loop at three in the morning.",
"acg:Venus:ASC":"Places on this line make you easier to like. You may come across as charming, relaxed and better dressed than you intended, and your own sense of enjoyment grows. Living or travelling near it, pleasure and beauty feel close at hand. The shadow is comfort that slides into coasting.",
"acg:Venus:DSC":"Romance and friendship tend to come into focus near this line. The people you meet one to one are often kind, attractive and easy to be around, and agreements get settled with grace. Living or travelling here, notice whether you keep the peace by giving in more than you mean to.",
"acg:Venus:MC":"Charm and taste can shape your public standing. Fields touching design, hospitality, art, beauty or diplomacy may suit you, and colleagues often warm to your style. Living or travelling near it, you may be liked first and judged on results second, so let the work show too.",
"acg:Venus:IC":"A pretty, peaceful home life gathers around this line. Living or travelling near it often brings a love of making a space beautiful and a softer feeling with family. Quiet evenings, good food and gentle company restore you. The risk is avoiding hard family conversations just to keep the mood sweet.",
"acg:Mars:ASC":"Energy runs hot in places on this line. You may come across as direct, bold and ready to start, and your body wants to do something with all that drive. Living or travelling near it, courage is easier to find. Patience is the lesson, since impatience can shorten a temper.",
"acg:Mars:DSC":"Heat runs through one-to-one meetings near this line. You may attract people who are assertive, competitive or fiery, and debates can turn into sparring. Living or travelling here, the work is learning to disagree without needing to win, and to ask for what you want directly.",
"acg:Mars:MC":"Ambition sharpens in places on this line. Living or travelling near it, you may feel driven to compete, lead a team and make things happen fast, and your public image can read as forceful and decisive. Effort pays here, though bosses and rivals may push back, so pacing yourself keeps the drive sustainable.",
"acg:Mars:IC":"Restless energy lives under the floorboards near this line. Living or travelling here, you may feel an urge to renovate, reorganise or settle old family arguments. Home can feel charged and a little noisy. Physical work, a project or regular exercise gives that inner fire somewhere useful to go.",
"acg:Jupiter:ASC":"Optimism comes easily in places on this line. You may come across as generous, open and a little larger in spirit, and doors seem to open through friendliness. Living or travelling near it, faith in your own path can grow. The shadow is overdoing it: one more helping, one more promise, one more big plan.",
"acg:Jupiter:DSC":"Partners and the people you meet one to one tend to be generous, encouraging and well connected. Partners and collaborators may act as teachers, widening your view. Living or travelling here, watch for the habit of assuming it will all work out, and keep agreements specific.",
"acg:Jupiter:MC":"Public life favours a public role built on teaching, advising, publishing or leading with a big picture. Living or travelling near it, your reputation may grow through generosity and good timing, and mentors turn up. Stay honest about limits, since promising more than you can deliver wears down goodwill.",
"acg:Jupiter:IC":"A roomy, hospitable feeling settles around this line. Living or travelling near it, home may become the place where friends gather and meals run long, and family life can feel supportive and hopeful. Inner life grows through reading, belief and perspective. Clutter and extra weight of every sort are the thing to watch.",
"acg:Saturn:ASC":"Seriousness can settle over you along this line. You may come across as reserved, capable and older than your years, and it takes effort to relax. Living or travelling near it, discipline and focus come naturally, and slow progress earns real respect. Being kind to yourself matters here as much as being rigorous.",
"acg:Saturn:DSC":"Committed bonds matter here, and one-to-one relationships ask for commitment and clear terms. You may meet people who are older, steady or demanding, and bonds tend to be tested before they are trusted. Living or travelling here, the reward is lasting reliability. The lesson is not carrying the whole load for someone else.",
"acg:Saturn:MC":"Work gets taken seriously in places on this line. Living or travelling near it, you may carry responsibility early and build a reputation through patient, visible effort. Authority comes slowly but holds. The pressure to perform can feel heavy, so scheduling real rest is part of the job, not a reward for it.",
"acg:Saturn:IC":"Home and roots feel weighty near this line. Living or travelling here, you may think about duty to family, the age of the house or what you inherited emotionally. Building a stable base takes effort, and that effort tends to last. Letting warmth in matters as much as keeping order.",
"acg:Uranus:ASC":"Unconventional is how you may feel in places on this line. You may come across as original, hard to categorise and a little unpredictable, and routines loosen. Living or travelling near it, fresh ideas and a wish for freedom speed up. The edge is restlessness, so choose a few things worth staying with.",
"acg:Uranus:DSC":"Sudden, unusual meetings are common in one-to-one life near this line. You may attract independent, eccentric or very different people, and bonds that start with a spark can need plenty of space. Living or travelling here, honest talk about freedom keeps a partnership from feeling like a cage.",
"acg:Uranus:MC":"An unusual path in public life is favoured here. Living or travelling near it, you may find yourself in technology, reform, invention or any field that rewards being first. Your reputation can shift in jumps rather than steady steps. Flexibility helps, and so does finishing what you start.",
"acg:Uranus:IC":"Home feels unconventional near this line. Living or travelling here, routines at home may change often, and you may feel a pull to break from family patterns or try a different way of living. Inner life can be restless, with sudden insights. A small steady anchor makes the freedom easier to enjoy.",
"acg:Neptune:ASC":"Your edges soften in places on this line. You may come across as dreamy, sensitive and hard to pin down, and others may project ideals onto you. Living or travelling near it, intuition and imagination run high, and so does absorbing everyone's mood. Clear routines and honest boundaries keep the magic from turning hazy.",
"acg:Neptune:DSC":"One-to-one bonds can feel almost spiritual near this line. You may meet people who seem like soulmates, artists or those who need rescuing, and it is easy to see more than is there. Living or travelling here, ask plain questions and let actions, not feelings alone, show who someone is.",
"acg:Neptune:MC":"Public work that inspires, heals, creates or serves a larger ideal suits this line that inspires, heals, creates or serves a larger ideal. Living or travelling near it, you may be seen as imaginative or compassionate, though your direction can feel foggy. Career goals may need writing down on purpose, since vague ambitions drift away.",
"acg:Neptune:IC":"A dreamy, tender mood settles near this line. Living or travelling here, home may feel like a sanctuary, and quiet, water, music or prayer can nourish you. Family stories may grow blurry or idealised. Giving yourself solitude helps, while keeping the practical side of the household clear and written down.",
"acg:Pluto:ASC":"Intensity follows you in places on this line. You may come across as magnetic, private and a little formidable, and people sense depth before you say a word. Living or travelling near it, old habits can feel ready to shed. The work is using that force on yourself, not on others.",
"acg:Pluto:DSC":"Near this line, one-to-one meetings run deep. You may attract strong, secretive or transformative people, and bonds can feel all-or-nothing. Living or travelling here, power and trust become the real subjects. Honest talk about control, jealousy and boundaries turns that intensity into something lasting and mutual.",
"acg:Pluto:MC":"Public roles carry extra weight along this line. Living or travelling near it, you may be drawn to work that looks into hidden problems, restructures or rebuilds, and you may become known for resilience. Influence grows through persistence. Notice any urge to control the outcome, and let others hold part of it.",
"acg:Pluto:IC":"The deepest layers of family and memory stir near this line. Living or travelling here, you may uncover buried stories, clear out a home or rework your sense of where you come from. It is slow, thorough renewal rather than a quick refresh. Patient support from someone you trust helps."};
